			<div class="content" id="post-content-2344672">
									

<p>Because this will likely come up again, almost all of the poems are <em>katauta</em>. The last poem is a <em>chōka</em>. There are some inherent issues because the poems are written in English, but they're meant to be from native Japanese speakers. So there's some inherent lapses in logic, which I've decided to just roll with.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Why not vacate all houses within the area of effect and monitor the people whose deaths are predicted?</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not going to go too far into what ultimately will be a difference in how I perceive this iteration of the Foundation, but my thought is that the Foundation views a woman from the local &quot;university&quot; coming to visit a harmless old eccentric once a month or so being far less conspicuous and disruptive (and less cost-intensive) than mass relocation. Once could make an argument, logically, for &quot;jail the shit out of everyone,&quot; and indeed I've written articles prior from that perspective. I choose to take a different direction here.</p>
<p>Thanks for reading.</p>

